{% comment %}
  InstaMom University — "add some extras?" modal.

  Opens automatically after a PACKAGE is added to the cart, and on demand from
  the "Add-ons" button on a package's cart line. Rendered once in
  layout/theme.liquid so it is available wherever an add-to-cart can happen.

  The add-on list is rendered server-side from the `add-ons` collection — no
  fetch, so there is no request to fail. Stock is respected: an add-on that is
  unavailable renders as a disabled "Sold out" button rather than being hidden,
  so the lineup always reads the same.

  data-package-ids carries the package product ids so the script can tell a
  package add (open the modal) from an add-on add (don't re-open it).

  Styling: .instamom-addons* in assets/instamom.css
  Behaviour: assets/instamom-addons.js
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign addons = collections['add-ons'].products -%}
{%- if addons.size > 0 -%}
  {%- capture package_ids -%}
    {%- for p in collections['packages'].products -%}{{ p.id }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  <modal-dialog
    id="InstamomAddons"
    class="instamom-addons"
    data-package-ids="{{ package_ids | strip }}"
  >
    <div
      role="dialog"
      aria-modal="true"
      aria-label="Add extras to your box"
      class="instamom-addons__content"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      <button
        id="ModalClose-InstamomAddons"
        type="button"
        class="instamom-addons__close"
        aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}"
      >
        {{- 'icon-close.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      </button>

      <h2 class="instamom-addons__title">Add a little extra?</h2>
      <p class="instamom-addons__intro">
        Customize your student's package with extra treats just for them.
      </p>

      <ul class="instamom-addons__grid" role="list">
        {%- for addon in addons -%}
          {%- assign variant = addon.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: addon.variants.first -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            No image. Owner, Aug 2026: "Add ons should not have photos, remove
            them from the template."

            This reverses the earlier review note ("Can the add-on boxes be more
            visually interesting? Maybe use our second level logo here?"), which
            is why these cards used to carry the IMU cap mark on a tinted panel
            as a stand-in for the product photos none of the add-ons has. Don't
            reinstate it from that older note — the cards are now type-only by
            request, and repeating one logo down nine cards was reading as noise
            anyway (the same reason the homepage add-ons LIST never used it).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <li class="instamom-addons__item">
            <span class="instamom-addons__name">{{ addon.title | escape }}</span>
            {%- comment -%}
              The `custom.cute_note` wink ("Trust us!"), kept out of the product
              title itself — see sections/instamom-addons-list.liquid.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign cute_note = addon.metafields.custom.cute_note.value -%}
            {%- if cute_note != blank -%}
              <span class="instamom-addons__aside">{{ cute_note | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <span class="instamom-addons__price">+{{ addon.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
            {%- render 'instamom-addon-contents', addon: addon -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="button button--secondary instamom-addons__add"
              data-variant-id="{{ variant.id }}"
              {% unless variant.available %}
                disabled
              {% endunless %}
            >
              {%- if variant.available -%}
                {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}
              {%- else -%}
                {{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}
              {%- endif -%}
            </button>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

      {%- comment -%}
        Roommate gift-wrap instruction (owner review). Saved as the CART NOTE
        rather than a line-item property: the request ("wrap the snack sleeve
        separately for roommate Sarah") is an instruction to the packers about
        the order as a whole, and add-ons are added one at a time here, so
        there's no single line to hang it on. instamom-addons.js persists it on
        change/blur and again before the modal closes.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="instamom-addons__roommate">
        <label class="instamom-addons__roommate-label" for="InstamomRoommateNote">
          Buying an add-on for your student&rsquo;s roommate? You&rsquo;re so kind!
          If you&rsquo;d like for us to wrap it separately, please tell us which
          item(s), and share the roommate&rsquo;s name.
        </label>
        <textarea
          id="InstamomRoommateNote"
          class="instamom-addons__roommate-input"
          rows="2"
          data-roommate-note
          placeholder="e.g., Please wrap the extra snack sleeve separately for roommate Sarah."
        >{{ cart.note }}</textarea>
        <span class="instamom-addons__roommate-saved" data-roommate-saved hidden>Saved ✓</span>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The way out has to move the shopper FORWARD. This button used to read
        "No thanks, continue" and only call modal.hide(), which dropped them
        back on the product page they came from with no checkout in sight — the
        add-to-cart notification that carries Dawn's "Check out" button is
        underneath this modal and gone by the time it closes. Shoppers read
        "continue" as "continue to checkout", hit it, landed back on the box,
        and went round again.

        It goes to the CART, not straight to /checkout, because the cart page
        is where the required candy preference and Terms agreement live (see
        sections/main-cart-footer.liquid and snippets/instamom-terms-agree.liquid).
        Jumping the shopper past those would skip the allergy answer and the
        agreement the Terms themselves say is given by ticking that box.

        Opened from a cart line's "+ Add-ons" trigger there's nowhere to go, so
        the button just closes — hence the two labels.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="instamom-addons__actions">
        {%- if template.name == 'cart' -%}
          <button type="button" class="button instamom-addons__skip" data-close-only>
            Done
          </button>
        {%- else -%}
          <button type="button" class="button instamom-addons__skip">
            No thanks, take me to my cart
          </button>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </modal-dialog>
{%- endif -%}
